 for name,v in broad.items():lines.append(f"| {name} | {v['target_context_pairs']} | {v['equal_study_raw_PDS_change']:+.6f} |")
 lines+=['', 'This uses every target with at least 30 real cells in existing extractions: 25 H1, 282 HCT116, 291 HEK293T, 23 resting CD4 and 34 stimulated CD4. All 300 panel genes are excluded from the geometry. The predicted side contains intended pooled means before cell rounding. This establishes a broader mean-identity trade-off, not complete competition performance. The guard preserves model geometry and reduces the broader identity loss, but does not guarantee agreement with measured truth.','', '## What this supports','', 'Changing response representation improves expression-error diagnostics more consistently than the rejected state-composition transfer. The target-identity trade-off remains unresolved. The separately frozen V64 scalar-only follow-up also failed its count gates; see V64_RESULTS.md. Case replication and corrected unique-label scoring are audited in V62_V64_VALIDATION_AUDIT.md. This artifact is a controlled experiment to measure that trade-off on the hidden scorer. It should not be described as a significant ranking improvement before the hosted result exists. V24 remains the fallback.','', 'All source studies, public mean labels and many raw count cases have been examined repeatedly in earlier work. No new independent study or D3 donor was opened. The unchanged generator still creates excessive control-null DE compared with real controls; the new guard does not solve that issue. All six official anchor scales remain unknown. The mapped source profiles cover roughly 68%-100% of a per-cell CPM library and are used without reclosure; the initial source-plan word closed was inaccurate. Query profiles are aligned-axis normalized. These are incomplete-axis per-cell proxies rather than exact shared-axis pooled profiles; source_normalization_audit.json records the actual coverage and this limitation. No predictor was changed after that audit.','', '## Upload artifact and verification','',f"Path: `experiments/v63_identity_guard/prediction.vcc` ({ready['bytes']:,} bytes). SHA256 `{ready['sha256']}`. Official prep passed; 360,000 cells, 18,533 genes, 900 target/context groups and 400 cells/group verified. Every packaged sparse value/index/pointer and all axes match the generated counts. Every original control cell ID, guide and library is checked; 12 complete groups are regenerated exactly. All 900 response vectors replay, and the production-margin inequalities receive an independent per-target check. These are integrity checks, not proof of hidden accuracy.",'', 'The original pre-upload receipts and failed-gate records remain unchanged. Use [V63_SUBMISSION.md](V63_SUBMISSION.md) for the CMD command. Root scripts and compact provenance are committed locally. No automatic upload or Git push.']
 lines+=['','## Visual trade-off','', '![V63 error and identity trade-off](experiments/v63_identity_guard/analysis/tradeoff.png)','', 'The two panels use different public cohorts and are not official scaled scores.']
